  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO: Contributing to more transparent and inclusive electoral process through 2024 Parliamentary elections observation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project implemented by Georgian Young Lawyers&#x2019; Association is designed to bolster the transparency, fairness, and overall integrity of the electoral process in the country through the observation of elections by independent and objective watchdog organisation. With a total of 600 observers set to be deployed across the nation, this specific project aims to support 150 of these observers through comprehensive training programs and deploy them on the election day. Moreover, the project will cover the pre-election, e-day and post-election period to assess overall organisation of electoral process in Georgia. Georgian Young Lawyers&#x2019; Association&#x2019;s observation mission will consist of: 80 precinct, precinct perimeter, and mobile group observers, 30 district observers, 40 headquarters members. Georgian Young Lawyers&#x2019; Association will also litigate cases on problematic areas in elections apparent through the short-term and long-term missions. Based on the findings of the election observation mission and in parallel with it, Georgian Young Lawyers&#x2019; Association will continue advocating its recommendations to the decision-making bodies (Central Election Commission and the Parliament) to improve the electoral system in Georgia.</narrative>
  </description>
